3uq|n|Separately, in regard to space or company; in a state of separation as to place; aside. ; In a state of separation, of exclusion, or of distinction, as to purpose, use, or character, or as a matter of thought; separately; independently; as, consider the two propositions apart. ; Aside; away. ; In two or more parts; asunder; to piece; as, to take a piece of machinery apart.	a:9a2,37,1;ze7,18,3;xtc,16,2;eah,3,1~ze7,18,3;xtc,16,2;9a2,37,1;eah,3,1	v:rll,44,1;24mr,28,2;eah,26,5;22gm,16,5~eah,26,5;22gm,16,5;24mr,28,2;rll,44,1	n:rl1,37,2;lwi,21,2;rcd,13,5;xtc,6,1;22gm,3,2~rcd,13,5;rl1,37,2;lwi,21,2;22gm,3,2;xtc,6,1
